00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.951
The only thing I do remember is,

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:20.754 size:84% position:42%
I was standing under
the bleachers with Aidy

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:24.090
when Don Pardo announced
our names, and it was like,

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, now it´s real."
-Yeah.

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:26.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If I´m in the credits...
-No, right.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
Once you´re in the credits,
they have to give you a check.

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:30.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Even if I´m not in the show,
I´m in the damn credits.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.765
-Yeah.
-They give you that giant check.

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:33.566 size:75% position:38%
Or -- It´s this big.
-Yeah, that´s great.

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:34.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
You´ve got to go
to your bank and say,

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:37.003
"I need to cash my ´SNL´ check."
-Lorne goes with me, yeah,

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:39.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
he gives it to you.
-And are you excited --

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:41.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
You play Melania
on the show, beautifully.

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, thank you.
-Do you --

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:44.310 size:81% position:41%
Have you been watching
her over the summer?

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you looking forward
to playing her?

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:47.647
-She had, I think, top three

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:49.282
Melania moments over the summer.

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:51.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
She had, like, really hot hits
over the summer.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She crushed it
with some moments?

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:54.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She crushed at
a lot of silent moments,

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:57.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
like Melania´s silent
is just -- She´s so good.

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:59.993
And all of the hand things.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:02.228
I mean, she´s like a little cat.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:03.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, remember
the hand-swatting?

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:04.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, when he tried
to take her hand.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:09.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and she does it all
with such grace.

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.238 size:84% position:42%
-And doesn´t ever fall.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
It just like --
It looks like

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.209
it´s choreographed, almost.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:18.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then she took
her somber moment.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:21.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was my favorite picture,
was at the Wailing Wall,

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:23.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she´s in these red,
gorgeous heels, and, like,

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:27.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
this white suit,
and really taking her moment,

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:28.855
the sacred moment at the wall.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:31.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was like, "Yeah.
I get you, girl."

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:36.062
I can´t wait until there are
so many drag Melania Trumps.

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:38.731
I didn´t even think about that,
but that will be right up.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:39.732
-Oh, I´m thinking about it.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:40.934
That´s all I´m thinking about.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.903 size:81% position:41%
-Well, there´s a lot
of wonderful two-shots

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:46.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
of, you know,
he´s gesticulating,

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:50.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
and being sort of blow-hardy,
and she´s just aviators.

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:53.046
-She´s thinking about bullying.
-Yeah, oh, right.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:54.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
That´s her cause, is bullying.
-Yeah.

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:57.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you think she´s been
an effective champion

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:59.819
for the anti-bullying movement?

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:02.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
-As a real answer,
obviously, no.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:05.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Not in any -- on any Earth,

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:08.962
on any planet, but I´m going to
go ahead and say yes anyway,

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
´cause she´s --
That´s her thing.

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:12.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Do you think in the middle

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.267
of the night she ever leans over
to Donald and comes up with...

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.668
-She says like,
[ As Melania ] "I hate bullies."

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:18.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:20.039 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.107
[ Normal voice ] That´s her.

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:22.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
That´s her speech.

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:24.711
-She like, shakes him awake -- "

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.913 size:84% position:42%
[ As Melania ] Donald,
do you think it´s good?

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hate bullies.

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:29.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is good tweet?

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:30.917
[ Normal voice ]
Like she writes her own tweets.

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:33.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:35.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You --
So, you were at Second City.

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:36.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were an improviser
in Chicago.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you --
Did you kind of get

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:40.226
into Second City right away,
or were you doing improv shows

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.996
before that?
-So, when I was taking classes,

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:45.765
there would be like a couple
of the paid shows that we did

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:49.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
were all weird, and I did one
with my friend Paul.

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:52.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was -- It was like
a fashion show, I think,

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:54.240
but they wanted us to do improv.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s never a good idea.
-It was terrible.

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:57.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And it was like no one --

00:02:57.110 --> 00:03:00.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
No one was even listening,
and we just had to keep going,

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:01.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was awful.
And then finally when we got

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:03.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
to leave the stage,
there was no backstage

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:05.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
so we were trapped.

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:07.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we had to then go back on
to the stage to exit,

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:10.823
and at that point,
I just stood by the garbage can

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:12.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
and pretended to be
a garbage attendant,

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:15.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
to see if people would
even remember that I had been

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:18.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the stage, and if they --
And, like, people that

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:20.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
would assume that´s
a regular thing.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:23.436
This is so fancy, you can´t
throw your own trash away.

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:24.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you would...
-Give it to that girl

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:27.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a giant coat.

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:30.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You did child --
You were a child actor.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:32.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, you were
a stage child actor.

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:33.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, exactly.

00:03:33.947 --> 00:03:35.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What were those
early shows like?

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:38.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did a lot as the
Bailiwick Theater in Chicago.

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:40.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-And basically --

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a very,
also, gay theater.

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.790
So I was raised by so many
[ Audience member laughs ]

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
wonderful gays --
that really tickled you.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:47.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:50.196 size:84% position:42%
So, I was raised by all
these amazing gay men,

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:52.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was doing this show,
this family show called

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:55.335
"Christmas Schooner" and it´s
still going now in Chicago,

00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:57.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the late show that would
come in after us was

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:58.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Cyber Queer."

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:01.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I was, like, 11 years old,
and would skip off stage,

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:03.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there was just,
like, a giant man

00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:06.145
in little Speedo underpants
that´s like, "Hey, sweetie,

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:07.680
can I have my makeup table?"

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.148 size:78% position:39%
"Sure ´Cyber queer´!"

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:10.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.151
-Well, it must have been
a nice education, though.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:13.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was --
Oh, I wouldn´t trade it

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:14.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the world.

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:16.756
It really made me the gay man --

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:19.225
the cyber queer that I am today.

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:20.226
-Well, we´re lucky to have you.

